The short pages acts as my github notes for the quant project. It contains a list of commands and notes that I have found useful while working on the project. It is a work in progress and will be updated as I learn more about the project and the tools I am using.

Notes for terminal commands:
- To run the tests, use the command: `pytest`
- To run a specific test file, use the command: `pytest <file_name>.py`
- To run a specific test function, use the command: `pytest <file_name>.py::<function_name>`

to check the status of the git repository, use the command: `git status` and commit any changes using the command: `git commit -m "<commit_message>"`. To push the changes to the remote repository, use the command: `git push`.
